# Before adding a pattern that matches inside a source directory: ignoring a path
# keeps it out of tests/support/build.ts's source set, but not out of the mtime of
# the directory holding it, and every directory holding a source is read there. An
# untracked components/.DS_Store already reports the build stale naming the file;
# ignoring it makes the same run report `components/ gained, lost or renamed an
# entry`, which is harder to diagnose, not quieter. Patterns with no leading slash
# match at any depth, so this reaches further than the artifacts-at-the-root shape
# the list below happens to have today.

.superpowers/
node_modules
.output/
.wxt/
.worktrees/
test-results/
# @vitest/coverage-v8 is installed, so `--coverage` is one flag away. Untracked
# and unignored, its output would land in tests/support/build.ts's source set
# and report both builds stale — every build-reading test failing with a message
# about staleness rather than about coverage. A root-level artifact, like the
# rest of this list, which is what makes it safe: newestSource() excludes the
# repo root's own mtime.
coverage/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
